    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35385" root="قرأ" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَحِيفَةٌ مَقْرُوْءَةٌ</span></b> , (K, TA,) the only form of the
latter word allowed by Ks and Fr, (TA,) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْرُوَّةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْرِيَّةٌ</span>, (K, TA,) which are extr.,
except in the dial. of those who say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَيْتُ</span> [for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَأْتُ</span>], (TA,) [<i>A writing read.</i>]

